=== per-block interrupt-poll cost, in a translated loop (guest EL1) ===
  CNTFRQ_EL0 = 24000000 Hz

  Each section retires exactly 2,000,000 translated x86 instructions
  (1 x86 insn = 4 ARM ops; 40% memory-touching; 8 chained blocks/iteration)

  x86/blk       none    ld+cbnz   hdr-only   cbnz-reg    ld/blk%     hdr% reg/blk%
  5            500us       498us       500us       497us     -0.38%   +0.13%   -0.55%
  10           499us       497us       499us       497us     -0.29%   +0.03%   -0.33%
  20           498us       497us       503us       498us     -0.16%   +0.91%   -0.08%
  40           498us       518us       514us       498us     +3.97%   +3.34%   +0.04%
  80           505us       498us       499us       501us     -1.40%   -1.15%   -0.75%

  per-x86-instruction cost, and per-check cost in ns:
  x86/blk ns/x86insn  ns/ld-check ns/reg-check
  5           0.250       -0.005       -0.007
  10          0.249       -0.007       -0.008
  20          0.249       -0.008       -0.004
  40          0.249        0.395        0.004
  80          0.253       -0.283       -0.152

  drift control (same section run twice, k=5 and k=80):
    k=5  none 500us / 501us   ld+cbnz 498us / 498us  (-0.38% vs -0.56%)
    k=80 none 505us / 504us   ld+cbnz 498us / 492us  (-1.40% vs -2.39%)

  check-density slope: n checks inside every 5-x86-instruction block
  (400,000 blocks per section; slope = marginal ns per check)
  n/block    ld+cbnz us     ns/check    cbnz-reg us     ns/check
  0                 492       0.0000              -            -
  1                 491      -0.0034            497       0.0118
  2                 493       0.0004            499       0.0080
  4                 509       0.0102            512       0.0125
  8                 592       0.0311            629       0.0426
  16                958       0.0728            983       0.0766
  32               1900       0.1100           1886       0.1089
  baseline (n=0) measured twice: 492 us / 493 us  (drift +0.03%)

=== translated REP MOVSQ: how do you keep it interruptible? ===
  4096 elements x 512 repeats = 2,097,152 8-byte element copies per section
  strategy                            total    ns/elem   overhead worst-case IRQ
  no check (uninterruptible)          635us      0.303      +0.0%      unbounded
  load+cbnz every element             657us      0.313      +3.5%          0.3 ns
  load+cbnz every 8                   773us      0.369     +21.8%          2.9 ns
  load+cbnz every 64                  652us      0.311      +2.8%         19.9 ns
  load+cbnz every 512                 695us      0.331      +9.5%        169.6 ns
  cbnz reg every element              626us      0.299      -1.4%          0.3 ns
  no check (repeat)                   620us      0.295      -2.4%      unbounded

=== EL1 code-cache self-patch and timer-arm costs ===
  bare STR to the code page                          0.84 ns
  STR + DC CVAU + DSB ISH + IC IVAU + DSB + ISB    130.82 ns
  ISB alone                                          8.81 ns
  MRS CNTVCT_EL0                                     0.53 ns
  arm a deadline (MRS CNTVCT + MSR CVAL + CTL)       4.69 ns

  host exits during the whole run: 1
